<refentry id="systemd-machine-tags.service" conditional='ENABLE_HOSTNAMED'
          xmlns:xi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XInclude">

  <refentryinfo>
    <title>systemd-machine-tags.service</title>
    <productname>systemd</productname>
  </refentryinfo>

  <refmeta>
    <refentrytitle>systemd-machine-tags.service</refentrytitle>
    <manvolnum>8</manvolnum>
  </refmeta>

  <refnamediv>
    <refname>systemd-machine-tags.service</refname>
    <refpurpose>Apply the machine tags configuration at boot</refpurpose>
  </refnamediv>

  <refsynopsisdiv>
    <para><filename>systemd-machine-tags.service</filename></para>
  </refsynopsisdiv>

  <refsect1>
    <title>Description</title>

    <para><filename>systemd-machine-tags.service</filename> is an early boot service that applies the machine
    tag configuration declared in the <filename>tags.d/</filename> directories, see
    <citerefentry><refentrytitle>tags.d</refentrytitle><manvolnum>5</manvolnum></citerefentry>, by invoking
    <command>hostnamectl tags --apply</command>, see
    <citerefentry><refentrytitle>hostnamectl</refentrytitle><manvolnum>1</manvolnum></citerefentry>. The
    additions and removals declared there are applied on top of the tags already configured in the
    <varname>TAGS=</varname> field of
    <citerefentry><refentrytitle>machine-info</refentrytitle><manvolnum>5</manvolnum></citerefentry>.</para>

    <para>The service is ordered before <filename>sysinit.target</filename>, so that the configured tags are
    in place before most other units are started and may be used in their
    <varname>ConditionMachineTag=</varname> settings, see
    <citerefentry><refentrytitle>systemd.unit</refentrytitle><manvolnum>5</manvolnum></citerefentry>.</para>

    <xi:include href="version-info.xml" xpointer="v263"/>
  </refsect1>

